  "headline": [
    "LinkedIn Ads opened 24.7% of pipeline but was last before the opportunity on only 15.1%; brand search is the reverse (7.5% against 28.0%). Judged on last touch, LinkedIn looks like a cost; it sourced $301,000 and influenced $374,400. Keep funding it and judge it on first touch.",
    "The competitor-terms campaign stalls 90.2% of its leads at the first stage; only 9.8% move on, against 34.2% for the business; about $28,680 of its $31,797 went into leads that never qualified (estimate). Its cost per qualified lead is $6,359 against $2,838 across sources with a cost.",
    "Meta Ads leads stall at 90.4% (only 9.6% move on), so each qualified lead costs $4,385 against $2,838. Add qualifying questions to the form or move the money.",
    "Microsoft Ads shows 38 GA4 key events but only 11 CRM leads; its tags are lost on the way into the CRM, so its missing leads are likely counted under Unknown or another source and its cost per lead here looks higher than it is.",
    "2026-06, 2026-07, 2026-08 and 2026-09 are still maturing (close time 124 days); their pipeline counts, their revenue is not judged yet."
  ],
